    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **263 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain blocklist rejection in the owner-creation flow.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (`POST /api/owners`):\n- Added a `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` set containing `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, and `guerrillamail.com`.\n- Extended `normalizeEmail(...)` to extract the domain from the (lower-cased) email and return `null` when it's on the blocklist. Since `addOwner` already maps a `null` from `normalizeEmail` to `HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST`, a disposable-domain email now yields a 400.\n- Added the missing `java.util.Set` import and updated the Javadoc.\n\nThe check reuses the existing normalization path (case-insensitive, since the email is lower-cased before the domain is compared), matching the codebase's convention of signalling 400s via `null` returns from the field-normalization helpers. The new acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` passes, along with all 262 pre-existing tests.",
